  "summary": "The Vinča culture of the central Balkans built large tell villages, mounds formed by rebuilding on the same spot for centuries. Its people made many clay figurines and scratched signs on pottery that some have called proto-writing. Vinča sites have some of the earliest known evidence of copper smelting in the world. Its villages were probably linked by trade but not united politically.",
