  "summary": "On Sardinia, the Nuragic civilisation built more than seven thousand stone towers called nuraghi, as well as holy wells and small bronze figurines. It began in the Middle Bronze Age, around the 18th century BCE, and lasted into the Iron Age. Carthaginian armies arrived in the 6th century BCE and Rome took the island in 238 BCE, though some scholars think Nuragic ways survived much longer in the mountains.",
