  "summary": "The Hallstatt culture was the Early Iron Age culture of central Europe, named after the salt-mining site of Hallstatt in Austria. It is linked to early Celtic peoples. Iron tools and weapons spread, and powerful chiefs ruled from hillforts such as the Heuneburg, trading with Greek colonies such as Massalia (Marseille) for luxury goods. Some were buried in rich mound graves with wagons. It was followed by the La Tène culture.",
